WHAT hash-membership across complete object stores; HOW CERTAIN proven for byte-level content coverage (hash equality is definitive); WHAT-NOT-TESTED semantic/metadata uniqueness (a byte-covered file could still hold archival value out of context), backup .git pack internals beyond blob set (blob set does cover them).\n\n== 4. DEPENDENCY SWEEP (literal '/home/claude-code/projects/Tools') ==\n| Location | Hits | Classification |\n|---|---|---|\n| ~/.config/systemd/user/ | 0 | — |\n| /etc/systemd/system/ | 0 | — |\n| crontab -l | 0 (crontab exists, 1 line) | — |\n| ~/.bashrc ~/.profile ~/.bash_profile | 0 | — |\n| ~/.local/bin/* content | 0 | — |\n| Symlinks into Tools (~/.local/bin, ~/.config/opencode, ~/.claude) | NONE — claude/opencode/crosslink-moe are regular FILES, not links | stale-safe |\n| Sibling projects main trees | 27 | ALL doc/knowledge pointers: ASES docs/research Tools-Distribution reviews ×11 (historical design discussion of proposed symlink architecture — never implemented as symlinks), ASES .crosslink rules/knowledge-cache pointers to TOOLING.md ×8 (become dead links if repo deleted; not executable deps), ASES-backup ×2 (stale-safe), Tools-backup self-references ×6 (die with backup) |\n| Project worktrees | 73 | mirrored copies of the same ASES docs/rules across 6 worktrees — transient noise, stale-safe |\n\nLive-critical count: ZERO. Notable drift finding: ~/.local/bin/claude (2026-08-01) and opencode (2026-08-09) are NEWER than their Tools/scripts copies (2026-07-20 / 2026-07-09) — live operational wrappers have evolved past the repo; crosslink-moe identical. The repo no longer reflects live tooling state for 2 of 3 wrappers.\nClaim discipline: WHY deletion safety; WHAT literal-string sweep of all dispatched locations + symlink-table inspection + wrapper diffs; HOW CERTAIN evidence-based; WHAT-NOT-TESTED non-literal references (env-var indirection like $PROJECTS/Tools, string-concatenated paths, relative paths resolving into Tools), other users' crontabs, binary-file contents (skipped via -I).\n\n== 5. RECOMMENDED FINALIZE SEQUENCE ==\n1. Fix GitHub auth first — push/tag verification is currently impossible (token rejected). Blocking.\n2. Resolve the local-only commit be99438e (#105 docs fix): push it, or explicitly accept its loss. Do NOT delete/archive before this is resolved either way.\n3. Final-state commit: decide on dirty items — commit .claude/findings-interrupt-plugin.md + .opencode/command/interrupt.md if wanted; .crosslink runtime churn (.last-hydrated-ref, rules/global.md) can be committed or left; scripts/claude working-tree change should be reconciled with the NEWER ~/.local/bin copy (bin is ahead — consider back-porting bin→repo before archiving).\n4. Tag suggestion: archive/final-20260825 (or v1.0-archive) on the final commit after step 3.\n5. Tools-backup deletion: NOTHING blocks it except operator sign-off on abandoning the 2026-07-09 issues.db snapshot (only unique content; superseded by live DB). If in doubt, cp that one 176KB file into the archive before deleting the rest.\n6. After deletion, sweep the doc pointers (ASES .crosslink/rules/{knowledge,tooling}.md + knowledge caches) so 'crosslink knowledge show tooling' doesn't route to a dead path — per consolidation doctrine #462 these should retarget Observer #460's successor mechanism.\n\nVerdict summary: Tools repo is ARCHIVABLE after steps 1–3; Tools-backup is DELETABLE now modulo the single issues.db decision. No live-critical dependencies exist anywhere in the swept surface.","created_at":"2026-08-25T02:01:45.226619566Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:V+9A9aaGkP+spKnMc9mwUEgqctSKZr6jFoOHaY9n48Y","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgYePDhyVZNWzYKpaCt0NIsfnSf/jqx9cKOV+zr8lYtjQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAKoaNhc9B0SXKC3EQoVqXq5PWOtQS1nDx2gCS58Wp7h7BCZ8jjwTnXYFtSvSfA1O7JiDgJLIp7GfKZrwt+1knAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:V+9A9aaGkP+spKnMc9mwUEgqctSKZr6jFoOHaY9n48Y","sign